      "year": 1998,
      "director": "Histoire(s) du Cinéma – Part 3/3 Jean-Luc Godard",
      "description": "Jean-Luc Godard 's video series Histoire(s) du Cinéma , consists of eight episodes made over a period of ten years and is an extraordinary look at the medium through the eyes of this unique filmmaker. Hugely ambitious in scope, the series covers a wide range of topics from the birth of cinema to Italian neo-realism to Hollywood and beyond. JLG/JLG captures the complexity and brilliance of Godard’s work in film as it touches on a multitude of concerns, from memory and painting to the Swiss Alps, money and tennis.",
